The official win32 binary has the bitmap data available in PNG format for
use by plug-in window interfaces. The 32x32 tileset is stored in a file
called gltile32.png. It might be possible to convert this file to BMP
format and then configure the common controls interface to use it, but I
don't know how.

It would also be possible to build a BMP version of the 32x32 tileset from
the source, but there is no rule to do so in the Makefile provided so you
would need to modify it to add the following rule:

tiles32.bmp:	tile2bmp.exe ../win/share/mon32.txt \
		../win/share/obj32.txt ../win/share/oth32.txt
	tile2bmp $@ $(WSHR)\mon32.txt $(WSHR)\obj32.txt \
		$(WSHR)\oth32.txt

And then use:

C> mingw32-make tiles32.bmp

to create the file.

